@@ -70,6 +70,15 @@ The :meth:`~rich.console.Console.log` methods offers the same capabilities as pr
 To help with debugging, the log() method has a ``log_locals`` parameter. If you set this to ``True``, Rich will display a table of local variables where the method was called.
 
 
+Low level output
+----------------
+
+The :meth:`~rich.console.Console.out` method is a lower-level alternative to :meth:`~rich.console.Console.print` and :meth:`~rich.console.Console.log`. It converts each object to a string with normal string conversion, joins them with ``sep``, and writes the result followed by ``end``.
+
+Unlike print, ``out`` does not pretty print containers, wrap or crop text, render console markup, or replace emoji codes. It does apply automatic highlighting by default (set ``highlight=False`` to turn it off, or ``highlight=None`` to use the console default), and it accepts a basic ``style`` argument. Here's an example::
+
+    >>> console.out("[bold]Hello[/bold]", "World", sep=", ")
+
 Justify / Alignment
